questions.stem:
A crate counter runs this loop over an ArrayList<String> named crates holding ["fig", "date", "plum", "kiwi"]:
int total = 0;
for (String s : crates) {
  total++;
}
System.out.println(total);
What is printed?

A running club stores Runner objects with race times [Ana 55, Bo 42, Cy 61, Di 39] in an ArrayList<Runner> named club, then runs:
ArrayList<String> fast = new ArrayList<>();
for (Runner r : club) {
  if (r.getTime() < 50) {
    fast.add(r.getName());
  }
}
System.out.println(fast.size());
What is printed?

A forester maps tree names ["oak", "elm", "maple"] in an ArrayList<String> named words to their lengths:
ArrayList<Integer> lens = new ArrayList<>();
for (String w : words) {
  lens.add(w.length());
}
System.out.println(lens);
What is printed?

A ticket checker stores counts as Integer objects and runs:
Integer a = 200;
Integer b = 200;
if (a == b) {
  System.out.println("match");
}
On a typical setup nothing prints even though both hold 200. Which choice best describes the bug?

A sensor program keeps even readings from an int array holding [7, 4, 9, 2]:
ArrayList<Integer> evens = new ArrayList<>();
for (int n : readings) {
  if (______) {
    evens.add(n);
  }
}
Which blank collects exactly [4, 2]?

A bird survey stores ["heron", "ibis", "egret", "owl", "crane"] in an ArrayList<String> named birds, then runs:
int c = 0;
for (String b : birds) {
  if (b.length() > 4) {
    c++;
  }
}
What value does c hold? Respond with the integer only.

A swim coach totals laps stored as an ArrayList<Integer> named laps holding [3, null, 5]:
int total = 0;
for (Integer x : laps) {
  total += x;
}
What happens when this loop runs?

A tide crew removes negative readings from an ArrayList<Integer> named tides holding [4, -1, -2, 5] with:
for (int i = 0; i < tides.size(); i++) {
  if (tides.get(i) < 0) {
    tides.remove(i);
  }
}
After the loop, -2 is still in the list. Which choice best explains the outcome?

A travel list maps town names to capitals from a String array holding ["ely", "dover"]:
ArrayList<String> upper = new ArrayList<>();
for (String s : towns) {
  upper.add(______);
}
Which blank builds ["ELY", "DOVER"]?

A gift shop keeps order prices [12, 45, 30, 60] in an ArrayList<Integer> named orders, then runs:
ArrayList<Integer> boxed = new ArrayList<>();
for (int price : orders) {
  if (price >= 30) {
    boxed.add(price + 5);
  }
}
System.out.println(boxed);
What is printed?

A rain gauge totals an ArrayList<Integer> named drops holding [10, null, 4], where null marks a failed sensor:
int total = 0;
for (Integer x : drops) {
  total += x;
}
The loop throws NullPointerException on the null entry. Which fix correctly totals the good readings?

A fruit stand maps ["pear", "fig", "melon", "kiwi"] in an ArrayList<String> named fruits to word lengths, then adds the lengths:
int total = 0;
for (String f : fruits) {
  total += f.length();
}
What value does total hold? Respond with the integer only.

A Quilt class implements Comparable<Quilt> so quilts with fewer squares sort first:
public int compareTo(Quilt other) {
  ______
}
Which blank implements ascending order by squares?

A freight program orders Crate objects by weight with:
public int compareTo(Crate other) {
  return this.weight - other.weight;
}
Weights are int values and can sit near Integer.MAX_VALUE. Which choice best describes the flaw?

A nursery filters seedling heights [9, 3, 7, 4], subtracts 2 from each survivor, sorts ascending, and prints index 0:
ArrayList<Integer> kept = new ArrayList<>();
for (int h : heights) {
  if (h >= 4) {
    kept.add(h - 2);
  }
}
Collections.sort(kept);
System.out.println(kept.get(0));
What is printed?
